A||||17||BAM-BAM||Cross drilled rotors?||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||04-06-2000||10:59 PM||||    Has anyone, who has done the Baretta or Grand Am brake swap, ever had the rotors cross drilled at a machine shop? I was wondering if it has been done, and if it has what were the results. Just a thought <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>  Thanx,, BAM-BAM  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Standard||04-06-2000||11:39 PM||||Cross drilling really doesn't do much for a rotor, especially done that way.  All you will notice is stress cracking on the rotor between the holes.  <P>The only good way to get "cross drilled" rotors is to have the rotors cast with the holes in them, a la Porsche.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||04-07-2000||02:35 AM||||What about the Ocelot cross drilled rotors? Ive seen them in the Fiero Store Catalog for $370.00 a set. (84/87 part#56000)   <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">  any good????<BR> ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||04-07-2000||02:43 AM||||I have the Ocelot cross-drilled rotors. No problems yet. The cost from the Fiero Store includes all the brake pads too.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||04-07-2000||02:52 AM||||Oreif how long have you had them on your car?||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||04-07-2000||11:28 AM||||I fyou are looking for cross drilled rotors to improve braking? They won't. Experience has shown me that all cross drill rotors do is look good. I have cross drilled them myself, I have bought cross drilled rotrs and installed a few on customer cars. Unless you are going for looks and don't mind paying for it then get the cross drilled rotors, if you are going for better brakes don't spend your money, use it for sokething else which is more beneficial to you and your Fiero.Just my two cents of professional expertise.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||04-07-2000||11:52 AM||||I've had them since August of last year. Only difference is high speed stopping. If your going down the highway and need to stop quickly (tollbooth, idiot with a carphone,etc} You get no brake fade. Stopping distance is about the same normally. If you plan on racing it on road courses your brakes won't get overheated and fade out. As a daily driver they are no better than regular rotors but they do look good. The Fiero Store set is Only $40.00 more than buying stock rotors and pads from a local auto parts place.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Haze_Performance||04-07-2000||12:03 PM||||I would think that the fact that the stock fiero rotors are solid and the Ocelot's are two peice, in addition to being cross drilled, They should disapate heat faster than the stock ones there for the braking should be improved?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   ||||reg||5
Z||000008||Oreif||04-07-2000||12:08 PM||||The 88 cross-drilled rotors are 2 piece (vented) The 84 to 87 are solid rotors just like stock but cross-drilled. The ad is misleading because they show the 88 version.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Haze_Performance||04-07-2000||01:19 PM||||So the 84/87's are not vented? Hmmmmm! I quess its not worth it then.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <P>Thanks for the info...I almost ordered them...||||reg||8
Z||000010||Dan||04-07-2000||06:03 PM|||| Barretta upgrade-teriffic ---for half the price of stock||||reg||1
Z||000011||theogre||04-07-2000||07:48 PM||||HazeP, Bam bam, others,,<P>Search thru the old posts. I had a large responce to this once.....<P>In very short.<P>Drilling and grooving are done for waste management. They provide little if any cooling.<P>Only vented rotors have significant cooling improvment over plain solids.<P>Drilling you own rotors is perfectly fine if you know the metalergy of the rotor. That is what determins the size, placement, and after treatment of the drilling process.<P>Choice of pads used is as or more important than the rotor. Carbomets only work properly when hot. Semimets can fade if too hot but work fine for everything but racing. There are also ceramic based pads now. I don't know much about these. Raybestos claims they end brake dust staining. Don't know where they fit in the food chain but they are rated for regular street driving where carbomets have major problems.<P>The "grand am/bereta" upgrade provides better stopping primarily because these calipers have bigger pistons and more pad surface area. They gain fade resistance because the rotors are vented. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 04-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||lowCG||04-07-2000||09:25 PM||||If you're cooking your brakes,grooves or slots,not penetrating through the rotor,are the way to go.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Oreif||04-07-2000||09:46 PM||||I have been running carbomets for the last 3 years and have no problem with them. In fact I think they are much better than regular semi-metalics. I have used them for daily driving on all my vehicles and have not seen any problems hot or cold.||||reg||1
Z||000014||olympic||04-08-2000||03:22 AM||||   Cross drilling can also shorten brake pad life by 1/3.  But damn they look cool.   Choices, choices choices........||||reg||1
Z||000015||Haze_Performance||04-08-2000||04:35 AM||||I see that you are all full of brake info ....Anyone want to come over to my house and do my brakes???? Im a lazy S.O.B.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000016||BAM-BAM||04-08-2000||08:07 AM||||   Thanks everyone, I guess I picked a topic(again)of great preferential controversy. The only thing I can say is, I wanted to know what the advantages were in crossed drilled rotors and if it were practical to have it done yourself or buy them that way. There are far to many elements to consider in doing it myself and the expense of crossed drilled rotors verses the advantages in braking power makes purchasing them seem rather impractical; unless you have to have the "look". Thanks again, the info is greatly appriciated. I will do the upgrade to the Baretta brakes and leave it at vented rotors.<P> Thanx to all, BAM OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  ||||reg||7
Z||000017||GREENDANO||04-08-2000||01:19 PM||||I have surface drilled rotors that look like crossdrilled rotors on my F40 kit.  I drilled them when I was doing the GA brake swap.  I also have a picture of what it looks like through the wheel but PIP won't post my picture, so I'll have to try later.<BR>  Dan-O||||reg||1
